:true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":14},{"lap":3,"text":"On lap three, McLaren moved up to third when Ireland spun on oil at the end of the straight.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":3,"text":"\"I nearly went out of the race,\" he said. \"I went into a whirl, a 360-degree spin, cars were whipping past.\"","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0},{"lap":45,"text":"With puffs of smoke appearing from the left-side exhaust, the Cooper dropped back from Moss and finally entered the pits on lap 45.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":15},{"lap":59,"text":"However, his oil pressure was dropping, and on lap 59, the dark blue Lotus peeled off and retired suddenly, handing the lead to Ireland.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":14},{"lap":74,"text":"Hill was right on the tail of the Scot, hounding him for 15 laps, until he, too, suddenly coasted down the pit lane with a loose magneto wire.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":4},{"lap":97,"text":"With just over three laps remaining, Salvadori's privately entered Cooper blew its engine, just as his teammate John Surtees' car had done on the first lap.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":11},{"lap":100,"text":"Ireland came home under the waving checkered flag of Tex Hopkins, less than five seconds ahead of American Dan Gurney, as Britain's Tony Brooks finished the last GP of his career in third.","q":true,"src":"Wikipedia","c":0}],"x":{"drivers":[{"id":494,"ref":"ruby","name":"Lloyd Ruby","code":null,"nationality":"American","dob":"1928-01-12","helmet":null,"seasons":{"1961":{"car":"team_lotus_1961","source":"history","skills":{"pace":[0.0364,0.4026],"quali":[0.0964,0.2908]}}}}],"cars":[]}}